# What ships in the .vsix.
#
# vsce starts from every file of every production dependency and drops what
# matches a line here; a `!` line keeps a file even when another line drops it.
#
# The extension host is one compiled file (out/extension.js). The engine runs
# in a worker thread from node_modules/@gatetest/cli and is loaded file by
# file at runtime (src/core/registry.js requires each module by path), so it
# ships as files, never bundled.
#
# @gatetest/cli declares four dependencies; the scan path needs three:
#   acorn      — AST parsing (dead-code-extractor, direct-repair)
#   pixelmatch — visual-diff-engine
#   pngjs      — visual-diff-engine, and pixelmatch's own dependency
# The fourth, @modelcontextprotocol/sdk, is imported only by
# bin/gatetest-mcp.mjs, the MCP server, which the extension never runs from
# here (its "Configure MCP Server" command writes an `npx` command line). That
# one package pulls ~3,000 files (zod, hono, express, ajv, jose, ...) into the
# vsix, so node_modules is a whitelist: the engine and its three runtime
# dependencies, nothing else.
#
# test/packaged-vsix.test.js opens the built .vsix and proves that every
# engine module still loads from this layout and that a scan completes.
.vscode/**
src/**
test/**
tsconfig.json
*.vsix
**/*.map

node_modules/**
!node_modules/@gatetest/cli/package.json
!node_modules/@gatetest/cli/LICENSE
!node_modules/@gatetest/cli/src/**
!node_modules/@gatetest/cli/lib/**
!node_modules/acorn/package.json
!node_modules/acorn/LICENSE
!node_modules/acorn/dist/acorn.js
!node_modules/pixelmatch/package.json
!node_modules/pixelmatch/LICENSE
!node_modules/pixelmatch/index.js
!node_modules/pngjs/package.json
!node_modules/pngjs/LICENSE
!node_modules/pngjs/lib/*.js
